    "wikipedia_summary": "<i><b>Opuntia stricta</b></i> is a species of large cactus that is endemic to the subtropical and tropical coastal areas of the Americas, especially around the Caribbean. Common names include <b>erect prickly pear</b> and <b>nopal estricto</b> (Spanish). The first description as <i>Cactus strictus</i> was published in 1803 by Adrian Hardy Haworth. In 1812 he moved the species to the genus <i>Opuntia</i>.",
